menu "Nightglass audio"

config NIGHTGLASS_AUDIO_ENABLED
    bool "Enable audio input/output"
    default y
    help
        Enable the supervised ES8311/ES7210 diagnostic surface. The Audio app
        provides explicit bounded playback and microphone tests; no recording
        is stored or transmitted. Boot only arms the service with the PA gate
        low. Codec, I2S DMA, microphones, and the one-shot worker exist only
        during a user-initiated test. Disable this to omit the service.

config NIGHTGLASS_AUDIO_BOOT_SELF_TEST
    bool "Run one audio hardware self-test after boot"
    depends on NIGHTGLASS_AUDIO_ENABLED
    default n
    help
        Queue one bounded microphone capture followed by one bounded speaker
        tone after the normal Nightglass shell reaches ready state. Results
        are emitted to the serial log and no captured samples are retained.
        This is a bench/HIL gate only and must remain disabled in production.

endmenu
